S) in various soft lithography applications. PMMS stamps were made by cross-linking with triallyl cyanurate and ethoxylated (4) bisphenol A dimethacrylate via thiol\u2212ene mixed-mode chemistry. The surface chemistry of the materials was characterized by XPS when varied from hydrophilic through oxygen plasma treatment, to hydrophobic by exposure to a fluorinated trichlorosilane agent. The materials are transparent above 300 nm and thermally stable up to 225 \u00b0C, thus rendering them capable to be employed in step-and-flash imprint lithography, nanoimprint lithography, nanotransfer printing, and proximity-field nanopatterning. The successful pattern replication from the micrometer to sub-100 nm scale was demonstrated.","author_count":10,"author_ids":["A5007699390","A5012052318","A5020001579","A5045551635","A5064340656","A5078455808","A5109069954","A5109909868","A5111683427"],"author_institution_ids":["I154570441"],"authors":[{"id":"","name":"Luis M. Campos"},{"id":"A5007699390","name":"Tu T. Truong"},{"id":"A5111683427","name":"Dong Eun Erica Shim"},{"id":"A5078455808","name":"Michael D. Dimitriou"},{"id":"A5020001579","name":"Daniel Jay-Lee Shir"},{"id":"A5109069954","name":"Ines Meinel"},{"id":"A5012052318","name":"Jeffrey A. Gerbec"},{"id":"A5109909868","name":"H. Thomas Hahn"},{"id":"A5045551635","name":"John A. Rogers"},{"id":"A5064340656","name":"Craig J. Hawker"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":77,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1021/cm902506a","domain_tags":["analytical_methods","plastic_associated_chemicals","wastewater_and_treatment"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I154570441","I157725225","I161318765"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Chemistry of Materials","last_updated":"2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1875074","openalex_topics":["T11471","T11737","T12224"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"chemicals-in-plastics","primary_topic":"T12224","